Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 07:49:07 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] plugins/screentransform: Paint the whole snapshot of the old
 frame

Scene::paint() takes a region in device pixels, but the capture passes
the output's logical geometry. With a scale factor above 1 only the
top left part of the snapshot gets painted, e.g. 1171x878 of a
2048x1536 output at 175%. The texture is not cleared after
allocation, so the rest of it shows whatever the memory held before,
which looks like snow or stale pieces of old frames while the rotation
animation runs.

Paint the delegate's whole device rect instead.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UQSvSLBoFcFR7i6bQghXDu
---
 src/plugins/screentransform/screentransform.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/plugins/screentransform/screentransform.cpp b/src/plugins/screentransform/screentransform.cpp
index 93af452..b46cb7b 100644
--- a/src/plugins/screentransform/screentransform.cpp
+++ b/src/plugins/screentransform/screentransform.cpp
@@ -112,7 +112,7 @@ void ScreenTransformEffect::addScreen(LogicalOutput *screen)
         delegate.setViewport(screen->geometryF());
         delegate.setScale(screen->scale());
         scene->prePaint(&delegate);
-        scene->paint(renderTarget, QPoint(), screen->geometry());
+        scene->paint(renderTarget, QPoint(), delegate.deviceRect());
         scene->postPaint();
     });
 }
